Key Product Initiatives — Executive Snapshot 

Executive summary: Strong product momentum across onboarding, content creation, and platform build-out, but the narrative needs sharper quantified outcomes and explicit next decisions to be leadership-ready. 

Outcomes to date (as stated): approx 120 children onboarded via LO Assignment Wizard; 22 social stories created via Social Story Wizard.  

1) LO Assignment Wizard 

Why it matters: Therapists and teachers struggle to determine how to start assigning learning objectives (LOs), slowing onboarding and time-to-value. 

What it delivers: 

Questionnaire-based flow to define a starting set of learning objectives that can be assigned to a child. 

Compares questionnaire responses across multiple time periods. 

Supports multi-language. 

Shares questionnaires with a therapist or caregiver to complete at their convenience. 

Provides access for therapists from ce ntres to manage their own children independently. 

Generates reports using the child’s raw CBT data. 

Supports CBT branding and illustration usage in reports. 

Impact to date: 100+ children onboarded in 3 months. 

2) Social Story Wizard 

Enables creation of social stories using CBT illustrations and color styles. 

Supports multi-language (English and Arabic). 

Impact to date: 22 social stories created in 1 month. 

3) Lead Generation Initiatives 

Website “Try demo” experience to let prospects sample the platform and submit inputs. 

In-app “Try demo” for users who have downloaded the mobile app. 

Updated branding and logo plus App Store Optimization (ASO) for app and store listing text. 

4) Screening Platform 

Multi-modal screening (games + questionnaires) to suggest a child’s risk score. 

Next: Confirm validation approach and rollout plan (pilot sites, timeframe, and success criteria). 

5) Autism Therapy Center Platform 

Therapy center platform for patient inquiry, intake, enrollment, scheduling, billing, and ongoing engagement. 

Next: Define MVP engineering timelines  

 

